1
00:00:16,510 --> 00:00:41,480
 Stars, galaxies, in astral seas above, on cosmic paths we'll trace, man over wings.

2
00:01:28,930 --> 00:01:40,690
 Liberty is such a wandering thing, behind us all, come see, come take your place, we're

3
00:01:40,690 --> 00:02:04,330
 leaving soon for-

4
00:02:04,330 --> 00:02:21,420
 She's to say, for services above and beyond the call of duty performed by risk of life

5
00:02:21,420 --> 00:02:24,450
 and limb, I wish to award the order of merit with highest honors.

6
00:02:24,770 --> 00:02:25,790
 Not at all, not at all.

7
00:02:25,960 --> 00:02:27,360
 Any humanoid would have done the same thing.

8
00:02:27,360 --> 00:02:31,600
 And of course, in honoring Metro, we can only reflect glory on his creator,

9
00:02:32,010 --> 00:02:35,010
 our universally renowned, inimitable Professor Maestro,

10
00:02:35,310 --> 00:02:37,450
 the most brilliant mind in all our confederation.

11
00:02:37,830 --> 00:02:41,490
 What's he got to do with this anyway? He didn't do anything. He's a big thinker.

12
00:02:41,670 --> 00:02:45,610
 And now, let us lift our glasses to our newly promoted Captain Pirro,

13
00:02:45,900 --> 00:02:49,490
 who has earned this promotion through his exceptional courage and intelligence.

14
00:02:49,850 --> 00:02:50,850
 Thank you, Captain Pirro.

15
00:02:51,550 --> 00:02:55,710
 Youngest officer ever to hold such a high rank in the confederation. We're proud of you.

16
00:02:55,710 --> 00:02:58,640
 As for Lieutenant Pettigrew, our own slugger,

17
00:02:58,960 --> 00:03:02,270
 Your new insignia of full lieutenant bears witness to your devotion to duty,

18
00:03:02,750 --> 00:03:06,310
 to your courage, which you have demonstrated in every performance of duty.

19
00:03:06,690 --> 00:03:07,650
 We are proud of you, lieutenant.

20
00:03:07,890 --> 00:03:09,550
 I'm sure the great of captain isn't far away.

21
00:03:11,070 --> 00:03:13,430
 I have reserved for the last honors,

22
00:03:13,590 --> 00:03:16,650
 Lieutenant Mercedes, affectionately known to us all as Psyche,

23
00:03:16,650 --> 00:03:19,350
 by using her absolutely extraordinary powers,

24
00:03:19,470 --> 00:03:22,930
 which have so often transformed certain defeat into brilliant victory.

25
00:03:23,350 --> 00:03:25,970
 She has shown coolness and courage in the face of danger.

26
00:03:26,430 --> 00:03:29,870
 Her youth and apparent fragility disguise an indomitable will.

27
00:03:31,180 --> 00:03:33,980
 May you go on to serve as an example to other young women.

28
00:03:34,460 --> 00:03:36,790
 You may be sure that a brilliant career lies ahead of you.

29
00:03:37,040 --> 00:03:39,780
 Who can say how grateful our confederation may be one day?

30
00:03:40,110 --> 00:03:43,900
 All our very best wishes to you, Psyche, and our hope for your continued success.

31
00:03:44,660 --> 00:03:45,500
 Looking at her.

32
00:03:45,620 --> 00:03:46,800
 Oh, awesome, Psyche.

33
00:03:46,800 --> 00:03:47,700
 Yeah, sure right.

34
00:03:48,510 --> 00:03:48,990
 Hooray!

35
00:03:50,650 --> 00:03:53,820
 Apologies, sir. Urgent message from Leto.

36
00:03:54,120 --> 00:03:55,140
 Just a moment, please.

37
00:03:55,650 --> 00:03:57,680
 That's enough solemn ceremony.

38
00:03:57,880 --> 00:04:00,160
 Now our youngsters have earned a good time.

39
00:04:00,460 --> 00:04:02,760
 It's time for music with the Omega Group.

40
00:04:08,860 --> 00:04:16,030
 We did it, didn't we?

41
00:04:16,260 --> 00:04:17,460
 We? What do you mean, we?

42
00:04:18,010 --> 00:04:19,880
 We's right behind you.

43
00:04:20,230 --> 00:04:21,830
 Yes, that is a good place for you.

44
00:04:21,930 --> 00:04:25,170
 Just make sure that you're far enough back so that you don't get in my way.

45
00:04:28,710 --> 00:04:32,000
 And the colonel's waiting for you.

46
00:04:32,300 --> 00:04:32,990
 Excuse me.

47
00:04:34,550 --> 00:04:37,770
 The youngsters have earned a rest, some relaxation.

48
00:04:38,420 --> 00:04:41,070
 They've been in strenuous action for many months now.

49
00:04:41,070 --> 00:04:44,490
 After all, we have several other crews who are competent.

50
00:04:44,850 --> 00:04:46,110
 But they were requested.

51
00:04:46,450 --> 00:04:49,830
 They expressly said that's the crew, including Metro, that they wanted.

52
00:04:50,500 --> 00:04:52,070
 Very strange.

53
00:04:52,830 --> 00:04:54,830
 Yes. Well, they form a united team.

54
00:04:54,990 --> 00:04:57,630
 Why don't we ask them what they think? They're concerned?

55
00:04:57,920 --> 00:05:00,060
 You recall your adventures on the planet Leto?

56
00:05:00,220 --> 00:05:01,180
 I beat Golden Bar.

57
00:05:01,710 --> 00:05:04,680
 It appears new trouble's broken out. It's all very strange.

58
00:05:04,760 --> 00:05:07,400
 As I understand it, this time it's the men who have revolted.

59
00:05:07,400 --> 00:05:09,680
 At least that's what I gather from their message.

60
00:05:10,080 --> 00:05:14,200
 There's been a kind of ceasefire between men and robots awaiting your arrival.

61
00:05:14,580 --> 00:05:20,750
 But what makes the whole situation peculiar is they're expressly requesting that we send one certain individual, Metro.

62
00:05:21,170 --> 00:05:22,190
 But why him?

63
00:05:22,480 --> 00:05:25,760
 Oh, I don't see anything so unusual in that. I taught them a good lesson.

64
00:05:27,020 --> 00:05:28,880
 Anyway, the three of you form a team.

65
00:05:29,170 --> 00:05:32,720
 You know, you don't have to go if you don't want to. You're technically on leave.

66
00:05:33,030 --> 00:05:35,050
 Oh, you needn't trouble these two. I'll go alone.

67
00:05:35,690 --> 00:05:37,720
 Now you think you can pilot a spaceship?

68
00:05:37,820 --> 00:05:42,790
 Now all that is just routine, an hour or two, and I know I'll be ready to handle any ship.

69
00:05:43,370 --> 00:05:46,550
 I think it'll be all right, Madame President. You agree, Piero?

70
00:05:46,930 --> 00:05:48,350
 We had a good rest on Earth.

71
00:05:48,490 --> 00:05:49,250
 I feel great.

72
00:05:49,390 --> 00:05:51,250
 And we always work best as a team, right?

73
00:05:53,690 --> 00:06:05,440
 Here we are again, the three of us, just like the good old days.

74
00:06:05,740 --> 00:06:08,920
 You know, it's a little sad to think it's one of our last missions in this ship.

75
00:06:09,230 --> 00:06:10,490
 Our good old hummingbird.

76
00:06:11,150 --> 00:06:13,940
 Pretty soon, Captain, you'll be commanding a cruiser.

77
00:06:14,200 --> 00:06:15,600
 And when that happens, Lieutenant,

78
00:06:16,270 --> 00:06:18,950
 all that will remain is to select a second in command.

79
00:06:19,070 --> 00:06:19,710
 I guess you'll do.

80
00:06:20,240 --> 00:06:22,180
 And I will go on just checking circuits.

81
00:06:22,240 --> 00:06:22,500
 Ho-hum.

82
00:06:22,500 --> 00:06:26,240
 An android decorated with the Order of Merit is meant for higher things.

83
00:06:26,600 --> 00:06:27,240
 Quite right.

84
00:06:27,500 --> 00:06:29,420
 Metro, you will be up here in a command post.

85
00:06:29,570 --> 00:06:32,740
 And that means you'll be able to get us out of trouble more and more.

86
00:06:33,180 --> 00:06:36,960
 And for openers, it looks like you're going to run the show in this operation.

87
00:06:37,220 --> 00:06:38,880
 Kind of funny they ask for you, isn't it?

88
00:06:39,220 --> 00:06:40,700
 I don't think it's so strange.

89
00:06:41,000 --> 00:06:44,660
 I would just remind you I was rather impressive against their golden bar.

90
00:06:44,760 --> 00:06:47,080
 I think these ambulating junkyards would agree.

91
00:06:48,930 --> 00:06:51,110
 Planet Leto approaching.

92
00:06:51,630 --> 00:06:53,900
 And they did all they could to assist your landing.

93
00:06:54,360 --> 00:06:55,870
 Well, I don't understand it at all.

94
00:06:55,930 --> 00:06:56,950
 I wouldn't have expected it.

95
00:06:57,330 --> 00:06:59,830
 Ah, I think they were delighted to see us again.

96
00:07:00,270 --> 00:07:02,110
 They were delighted to see Metro again.

97
00:07:02,110 --> 00:07:06,350
 couldn't take their eyes off him it's true your exploits are known everywhere you're a star around

98
00:07:06,350 --> 00:07:11,250
 here metro can we get back to the situation governor what's wrong and why this revolt since

99
00:07:11,250 --> 00:07:16,520
 your departure the robot scene has been exemplary they've respected the treaty scrupulously in fact

100
00:07:16,520 --> 00:07:21,040
 they went overboard couldn't do enough for us very kind gentle even friendly as if they wanted

101
00:07:21,040 --> 00:08:25,970
 to shield us from any unpleasantness any effort at first we liked it everything for us on

102
00:08:25,970 --> 00:08:31,600
 construction sites and they worked at least as well as we could in the end it was boring however

103
00:08:31,600 --> 00:08:51,600
 every time we tried to complain they'd give us yet another toy. We began to wonder if they weren't

104
00:08:51,600 --> 00:08:57,540
 trying to sap our energy. What really shattered us was the boredom. Still, you went along with it.

105
00:08:57,540 --> 00:09:02,770
 No complaints were received on Omega. Yes, it's true. And even now I wonder where we found the

106
00:09:02,770 --> 00:09:08,630
 energy to stage any kind of revolt at all. Where did it start? We have a certain place just outside

107
00:09:08,630 --> 00:09:13,950
 the city. Well, in old ruins, neoclassical architecture, Doric. We call it our Acropolis.

108
00:09:13,950 --> 00:09:19,060
 I suppose we don't have many people here who know why it's called that. It's always been a symbol for

109
00:09:19,060 --> 00:09:21,050
 A tradition of liberty and democracy.

110
00:09:21,050 --> 00:09:23,410
 Man, the measure of all things.

111
00:09:23,410 --> 00:09:25,600
 A kind of myth, I suppose.

112
00:09:25,600 --> 00:09:28,110
 Families would go there on holidays.

113
00:09:28,110 --> 00:09:30,680
 Of course it was in ruins.

114
00:09:30,680 --> 00:09:32,770
 But when Robot Supreme decided to level it,

115
00:09:32,770 --> 00:09:35,270
 to put up some new project,

116
00:09:35,270 --> 00:09:37,270
 though it was useless, we fought them

117
00:09:37,270 --> 00:09:39,560
 with whatever few arms we still had.

118
00:09:39,560 --> 00:09:42,420
 It was suicide. They outnumbered us ten to one.

119
00:09:42,420 --> 00:09:45,150
 They went on being nice to us.

120
00:09:45,150 --> 00:09:47,150
 They refused combat, refused to annihilate us,

121
00:09:47,150 --> 00:09:49,270
 as they discreetly put it.

122
00:09:49,270 --> 00:09:51,270
 They said, "We are not your enemies."

123
00:09:51,270 --> 00:09:55,540
 Arbitrator, that's why you are here.

124
00:09:55,540 --> 00:10:01,410
 Supreme Liouzine is here for the delegation from Omega.

125
00:10:01,410 --> 00:10:10,940
 We're VIPs now, Metro, how's that?

126
00:10:10,940 --> 00:10:12,670
 No, it's no more than we deserve.

127
00:10:12,670 --> 00:10:46,410
 ...of a robot, his nobility.

128
00:10:46,410 --> 00:11:02,640
 We'll begin in a few moments.

129
00:11:02,640 --> 00:11:06,330
 Welcome to Tenant.

130
00:11:06,330 --> 00:11:09,510
 Polite Ladner.

131
00:11:09,510 --> 00:11:14,400
 And what is your side, Colonel?

132
00:11:14,400 --> 00:11:20,730
 ...creatures, we can find no other conclusion.

133
00:11:20,730 --> 00:11:21,890
 I will explain.

134
00:11:21,890 --> 00:11:25,740
 Create robots to serve you efficiently and well.

135
00:11:25,740 --> 00:11:28,620
 Then, when we carry out our tasks too well, you complain.

136
00:11:28,620 --> 00:11:29,760
 Only one conclusion.

137
00:11:29,760 --> 00:11:31,680
 We robots are rational, men are not.

138
00:11:31,680 --> 00:11:39,770
 They're all individuals. Unique. They're not machines. With them, it's judgment. Selection, proportion. You can't do that.

139
00:11:40,480 --> 00:11:43,760
 Changeable. What is most elusive is what interests him most.

140
00:11:43,970 --> 00:11:48,550
 Colonel, truer words were never spoken. Only why not let them choose what's good for them?

141
00:11:48,770 --> 00:11:50,910
 He is unable to maintain any choice.

142
00:11:51,440 --> 00:11:53,550
 Shouldn't he be allowed to change his mind?

143
00:11:53,770 --> 00:11:56,400
 We never change our minds. It is why we are superior.

144
00:11:57,480 --> 00:11:59,860
 Man has a sense of pleasure and displeasure.

145
00:11:59,860 --> 00:12:05,860
 But since these complex motivations are not integrated into your circuits, you cannot comprehend. You feel superior.

146
00:12:06,860 --> 00:12:09,180
 For you, we are no more than objects. Is that not right?

147
00:12:09,380 --> 00:12:12,260
 But the life we embody is as real to us as yours is to you.

148
00:12:12,430 --> 00:12:19,430
 And experience has proven that we are stronger, more competent, wiser than you are. In short, superior.

149
00:12:20,470 --> 00:12:23,230
 It's beginning to get on my nerves, this Colonel.

150
00:12:24,000 --> 00:12:29,620
 Why, you're no more than a tangled mass of wires, copper tubing, printed circuits, and plastic wrapped up in a metal shell.

151
00:12:29,620 --> 00:12:38,910
 You will allow me to remind you, sir, that you are made of the same, but since you insist on identifying yourself with your makers, I would point out that they are no different in theory.

152
00:12:39,090 --> 00:12:45,850
 They use slightly different materials, bits of carbon compounds, traces of metals, all inside a soft skin, so much for man.

153
00:12:46,240 --> 00:12:50,620
 Colonel, I find this discussion rather academic. Is it for this we were asked to come?

154
00:12:50,910 --> 00:12:55,710
 In our view, the old ruins called Acropolis are taking up space and serve no purpose.

155
00:12:55,710 --> 00:13:00,190
 We have decided to construct on the site an example of tomorrow's reality.

156
00:13:00,970 --> 00:13:03,720
 What reality? What terribly sad reality?

157
00:13:04,140 --> 00:13:05,890
 Listen once and for all.

158
00:13:06,190 --> 00:13:09,930
 Men are ready to fight for their ideals and traditions, and so are we.

159
00:13:10,170 --> 00:13:10,830
 What do you suggest?

160
00:13:11,150 --> 00:13:14,140
 Perhaps you recall your last visit to our planet.

161
00:13:14,280 --> 00:13:18,840
 To avoid decimating both sides, you suggested a single combat, chief to chief.

162
00:13:19,240 --> 00:13:20,940
 At present, we do not have weapons.

163
00:13:21,400 --> 00:13:25,590
 We know that we, the robots, are the stronger, but we do not wish to harm you.

164
00:13:25,590 --> 00:13:30,710
 we challenge you here and now will you accept such a fight champion against champion a fight

165
00:13:30,710 --> 00:13:37,400
 to the finish yes and then what the winner will dictate conditions but the fight will be divided

166
00:13:37,400 --> 00:13:43,160
 into two stages and to be declared winner he must win both stages not necessarily against the same

167
00:13:43,160 --> 00:13:48,230
 opponent if the first is unable to continue but then it's really two fights and i shall have to

168
00:13:48,230 --> 00:13:53,770
 fight both of them exactly don't you know our entire planet sings your praises knows how you

169
00:13:53,770 --> 00:13:55,690
 You felled our golden bar, the Invincible.

170
00:13:55,850 --> 00:13:58,510
 Now you will furnish us the opportunity to settle the score.

171
00:13:58,730 --> 00:14:00,330
 But I wouldn't call that fair.

172
00:14:03,130 --> 00:14:07,780
 Colonel, exactly why do you want this fight?

173
00:14:08,000 --> 00:14:09,640
 Let us say to prove our superiority.

174
00:14:10,420 --> 00:14:11,660
 Why, aren't you too sure?

175
00:14:12,140 --> 00:14:13,250
 Doubt is an emotion.

176
00:14:13,450 --> 00:14:14,650
 We do not possess emotions.

177
00:14:14,930 --> 00:14:18,510
 We consider demonstrated proof a more reliable guide to understanding.

178
00:14:19,170 --> 00:14:20,290
 One question, Colonel.

179
00:14:20,390 --> 00:14:21,350
 What are we waiting for?

180
00:14:21,730 --> 00:14:23,970
 Not awfully polite of your champion to keep me waiting.

181
00:14:24,410 --> 00:14:25,630
 Terribly sorry, sir.

182
00:14:25,630 --> 00:14:27,570
 But all things come to him who waits.

183
00:14:27,750 --> 00:14:28,350
 Here he is.

184
00:14:28,830 --> 00:14:33,620
 Our Battle Chieftain General Goldenbar II.

185
00:14:34,450 --> 00:14:37,040
 The delegation from Omega, I presume.

186
00:14:37,240 --> 00:14:40,560
 And this bit of tinsel, can this be the one I heard so much about?

187
00:14:41,190 --> 00:14:43,880
 Well, modestly, I might say, yes, it's me. How do you do?

188
00:14:44,170 --> 00:14:47,140
 How do you do? Now, I don't want there to be any disagreeable surprises.

189
00:14:47,440 --> 00:14:50,820
 Since our last meeting, there have been a few improvements on my side.

190
00:14:51,260 --> 00:14:56,230
 Our new beryllium-iridium alloy can attain a fusion temperature of 6,000 degrees.

191
00:14:56,470 --> 00:15:00,650
 Also, we are equipped with an ingenious built-in self-repair capability,

192
00:15:01,010 --> 00:15:04,470
 which instantly manufactures and attaches any elements that it may be damaged.

193
00:15:04,870 --> 00:15:09,090
 And would you believe we can reproduce ourselves at will whenever we deem it necessary.

194
00:15:09,390 --> 00:15:10,470
 Okay, fellas, back.

195
00:15:10,770 --> 00:15:12,730
 Now, what do you say to that mousetrap?

196
00:15:13,110 --> 00:15:14,110
 Very good, very good.

197
00:15:14,310 --> 00:15:16,670
 But it doesn't go very far, you know, not at all.

198
00:15:16,770 --> 00:15:17,830
 Now, tell the truth.

199
00:15:17,910 --> 00:15:18,650
 What else can you do?

200
00:15:19,070 --> 00:15:22,390
 Well, now that you ask, I have a brand new anti-gravity thing.

201
00:15:22,470 --> 00:15:23,450
 I can sort of fly.

202
00:15:23,610 --> 00:15:24,570
 Watch, I'll show you.

203
00:15:26,610 --> 00:15:35,740
 There you are.

204
00:15:35,840 --> 00:15:38,560
 An android forewarned is forearmed, they say.

205
00:15:38,560 --> 00:15:43,620
 But forearmed or backarmed, you're going to come to harm in the end, my own proverb.

206
00:15:43,820 --> 00:15:46,280
 What about your improvements? Are you too shy?

207
00:15:46,720 --> 00:15:51,870
 Eh, what's the use? You, Goldenboro, are obviously the greatest, the handsomest, the strongest, the cleverest.

208
00:15:52,780 --> 00:15:54,940
 Gentlemen, may the combat commence.

209
00:15:56,390 --> 00:15:59,100
 Hey, Goldie, if you'd rather be on this side, I don't mind.

210
00:16:00,940 --> 00:16:06,560
 Right, you say you're so crammed full of gadgets? Let's see what you can do, Goldie.

211
00:16:08,260 --> 00:16:17,330
 Guess who? I need new glasses. I'm seeing three.

212
00:16:19,910 --> 00:18:37,430
 Metro, squire, tell me you turn out quite a few like this.

213
00:18:38,030 --> 00:18:42,460
 Is this him? This spec? I didn't see this little thing.

214
00:18:42,770 --> 00:18:45,250
 Thing yourself, you bullying tower.

215
00:18:46,020 --> 00:18:52,170
 This second stage of combat, in order to keep the fight fair, we shall reveal the special capacities of the general.

216
00:18:53,460 --> 00:18:56,320
 Possesses no anti-gravity system. He does not fly.

217
00:18:56,980 --> 00:18:59,670
 Luckily, he possesses no regeneration capability.

218
00:19:00,530 --> 00:19:04,450
 No, the only faculty he does possess is one of reproducing himself.

219
00:19:04,450 --> 00:19:06,720
 But we don't consider that fair.

220
00:19:07,360 --> 00:19:09,300
 And he can duplicate himself all he wants?

221
00:19:09,700 --> 00:19:12,040
 No, he cannot. He is limited in his capacity.

222
00:19:12,220 --> 00:19:14,700
 So far, he can reproduce four alter egos in all.

223
00:19:14,940 --> 00:19:17,360
 But we are perfecting a new model much improved.

224
00:19:17,670 --> 00:19:19,930
 So, all together, I'll have to fight five of these guys.

225
00:19:20,370 --> 00:19:22,960
 It's not right. That's five against one.

226
00:19:23,680 --> 00:19:26,900
 It is possible for you to renounce combat at any time

227
00:19:26,900 --> 00:19:29,920
 and thus spare yourself any damage. You have only to ask.

228
00:19:30,420 --> 00:19:32,580
 That is something I wouldn't count on if I were you.

229
00:19:33,250 --> 00:19:35,580
 Don't you worry. I will be all right, I guarantee it.

230
00:19:35,580 --> 00:19:37,780
 However, as for all of those overgrown tin cans,

231
00:19:37,880 --> 00:19:43,340
 They are going to need quite a few space trains to carry away all the piles of junk that I am going to turn them into, and the sooner.

232
00:19:44,000 --> 00:19:46,790
 We're with you, Metro. Watch yourself. Don't get hurt.

233
00:19:47,420 --> 00:19:50,160
 When you've finished your little chat, maybe we can begin.

234
00:19:51,130 --> 00:19:53,690
 Gentlemen, are you ready? Let the combat commence.

235
00:19:58,540 --> 00:20:01,600
 Hey, you don't think you're going to get away with that again, do you?

236
00:20:03,850 --> 00:20:33,010
